    "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that&nbsp;passes through the points $left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis$ and $left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis$ has slope $m$, where $m equals StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction$, and can be defined by an equation of the form $y minus y 1 equals m left parenthesis x minus x 1 right parenthesis$. One of the lines shown in the graph passes through the points $left parenthesis 8 comma 0 right parenthesis$ and $left parenthesis 3 comma 4 right parenthesis$. Substituting $8$ for $x 1$, $0$ for $y 1$, $3$ for $x 2$, and $4$ for $y 2$ in the equation $m equals StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction$ yields&nbsp;$m equals StartFraction 4 minus 0 Over 3 minus 8 EndFraction$, or $m equals negative four fifths$. Substituting $negative four fifths$ for $m$, $8$ for $x 1$ and $0$ for $y 1$ in the equation $y minus y 1 equals m left parenthesis x minus x 1 right parenthesis$ yields $y minus 0 equals minus four fifths left parenthesis x minus 8 right parenthesis$, which is equivalent to $y equals minus four fifths x plus StartFraction 32 Over 5 EndFraction$. Adding $four fifths x$ to both sides of this equation yields $four fifths x plus y equals StartFraction 32 Over 5 EndFraction$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by $negative 10$ yields $minus 8 x minus 10 y equals negative 64$. Therefore, an equation of this line is $minus 8 x minus 10 y equals negative 64$. Similarly, the other line shown in the graph passes through the points&nbsp;$left parenthesis 8 comma 0 right parenthesis$ and $left parenthesis 3 comma 2 right parenthesis$. Substituting $8$ for $x 1$, $0$ for $y 1$, $3$ for $x 2$, and $2$ for&nbsp;$y 2$ in the equation $m equals StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction$ yields $m equals StartFraction 2 minus 0 Over 3 minus 8 EndFraction$, or $m equals negative two fifths$. Substituting $negative two fifths$ for $m$, $8$ for $x 1$, and $0$ for $y 1$ in the equation $y minus y 1 equals m left parenthesis x minus x 1 right parenthesis$ yields $y minus 0 equals minus two fifths left parenthesis x minus 8 right parenthesis$, which is equivalent to $y equals minus two fifths x plus StartFraction 16 Over 5 EndFraction$. Adding $two fifths x$ to both sides of this equation yields $two fifths x plus y equals StartFraction 16 Over 5 EndFraction$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by $10$ yields $4 x plus 10 y equals 32$. Therefore, an equation of this line is $4 x plus 10 y equals 32$. So, the system of linear equations represented by the lines shown is $4 x plus 10 y equals 32$ and $minus 8 x minus 10 y equals negative 64$.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>"
