    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">$2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis plus 4 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis equals 12$</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">$minus 2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis plus 4 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis equals 12$</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution to the given system of equations is $left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis$. What is the value of $8 x plus 7 y$?</p>",
    "options": null,
    "correctAnswer": "3",
    "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is $3$. Adding the second equation to the first equation in the given system of equations yields $left parenthesis 2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis right parenthesis plus left parenthesis 4 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis plus 4 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis right parenthesis equals 12 plus 12$, or $8 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis equals 24$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $8$ yields $7 y equals 3$. Substituting $3$ for $7 y$ in the first equation, $2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis plus 4 left parenthesis 7 y right parenthesis equals 12$, yields$2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis plus 4 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis equals 12$, or $2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis plus 12 equals 12$. Subtracting $12$ from both sides of this equation yields $2 left parenthesis 8 x right parenthesis equals 0$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $2$ yields $8 x equals 0$. Substituting $0$ for $8 x$ and $3$ for $7 y$ in the expression $8 x plus 7 y$ yields $0 plus 3$, or $3$. Therefore, the value of $8 x plus 7 y$ is $3$.</p>"
