    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction$</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the given function $f$, the value of&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis$ increases by $p percent sign$ for every increase of $x$ by $6$. What is the value of $p$?</p>",
    "options": null,
    "correctAnswer": "44",
    "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is $44$. For a function defined by an equation of the form $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction$, where $a$, $r$, and $k$ are positive constants, the value of&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis$ increases by&nbsp;$r percent sign$ for every increase of $x$ by $k$. The given equation can be rewritten as $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction 2 x Over 6 EndFraction$, or&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis left parenthesis 1.2 right parenthesis squared right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction$, which is equivalent to $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction$, or $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 44 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction$. This equation is of the form $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction$, where $a equals 27$, $r equals 44$, and $k equals 6$. It follows that the value of&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis$ increases by&nbsp;$44 percent sign$ for every increase of $x$ by $6$.&nbsp;Therefore, the value of $p$ is $44$.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Alternate approach: It's given that $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction$. An increase in the value of $x$ by $6$ can be represented by the expression $x plus 6$. The value of $f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis$ can be found by&nbsp;substituting $x plus 6$ for $x$ in the equation&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction$, which yields $f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x plus 6 Over 3 EndFraction$. By the product property of exponents, this equation is equivalent to&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript six thirds$, or&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis squared$, which can be rewritten as&nbsp;$f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis$. Since $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction$, it follows that $f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis dot left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis$. Therefore, for any value of $x$, the value of $f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis$&nbsp;is $1.44$ times, or $44 percent sign$ greater than, the value of $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis$. It's given that the value of $f left parenthesis x right parenthesis$ increases by&nbsp;$p percent sign$ for every increase in the value of $x$ by $6$. It follows that the value of $p$ is $44$.</p>"
