    "options": null,
    "correctAnswer": "38",
    "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is $38$. It&rsquo;s given that in rectangle $upper P upper Q upper R upper S$, the length of side $upper P upper S$ is $8$ more than the length of side $upper R upper S$. In a rectangle, opposite sides are congruent. Since side $upper Q upper R$ is opposite side $upper P upper S$, it follows that side $upper Q upper R$ is congruent to side $upper P upper S$. Thus, the length of side $upper Q upper R$ is $8$ more than the length of side $upper R upper S$. Let $x$ represent the length of side $upper R upper S$. It follows that the length of side $upper Q upper R$ is represented by the expression $x plus 8$. Since all angles in a rectangle are right angles, angle $upper R$ is a right angle. It follows that side $upper Q upper R$, side $upper R upper S$, and line segment $upper Q upper S$ form a right triangle, where line segment $upper Q upper S$ is the hypotenuse and sides $upper Q upper R$ and $upper R upper S$ are the legs. It&rsquo;s given that the length of line segment $upper Q upper S$ is $StartRoot 2,344 EndRoot$. By the Pythagorean theorem, if a right triangle has a hypotenuse with length $c$ and legs with lengths $a$ and $b$, then $a squared plus b squared equals c squared$. Substituting $x$ for $a$, $x plus 8$ for $b$, and $StartRoot 2,344 EndRoot$ for $c$ in this equation yields $x squared plus left parenthesis x plus 8 right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis StartRoot 2,344 EndRoot right parenthesis squared$, or $x squared plus left parenthesis x plus 8 right parenthesis squared equals 2,344$. Expanding the left-hand side of this equation yields $x squared plus x squared plus 16 x plus 64 equals 2,344$, or $2 x squared plus 16 x plus 64 equals 2,344$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $2$ yields $x squared plus 8 x plus 32 equals 1,172$. To complete the square, subtracting $16$ from both sides of this equation yields $x squared plus 8 x plus 16 equals 1,156$. Since the left-hand side of this equation is a perfect square trinomial, it follows that&nbsp;$x squared plus 8 x plus 16 equals 1,156$ is equivalent to $left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared equals 1,156$. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields $x plus 4 equals 34$. Subtracting $4$ from both sides of this equation yields $x equals 30$. Since the length of side $upper Q upper R$ is represented by the expression $x plus 8$, it follows that the length of side $upper Q upper R$ is $30 plus 8$, or $38$.</p>"
