    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that angle $upper Z$ in triangle $upper X upper Y upper Z$ is a right angle. Thus, side $upper Y upper Z$ is the leg opposite angle $upper X$ and side $upper X upper Z$ is the leg adjacent to angle $upper X$. The tangent of an acute angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the leg opposite the angle to the length of the leg adjacent to the angle. It follows that $tangent upper X equals StartFraction upper Y upper Z Over upper X upper Z EndFraction$. It's given that $tangent upper X equals StartFraction 12 Over 35 EndFraction$ and the length of side $upper Y upper Z$ is $24$ units. Substituting $StartFraction 12 Over 35 EndFraction$ for $tangent upper X$ and $24$ for $upper Y upper Z$ in the equation $tangent upper X equals StartFraction upper Y upper Z Over upper X upper Z EndFraction$ yields $StartFraction 12 Over 35 EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 Over upper X upper Z EndFraction$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by $35 left parenthesis upper X upper Z right parenthesis$ yields $12 left parenthesis upper X upper Z right parenthesis equals 24 left parenthesis 35 right parenthesis$, or $12 left parenthesis upper X upper Z right parenthesis equals 840$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $12$ yields $upper X upper Z equals 70$. The length $upper X upper Y$ can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem, which states that if a right triangle has legs with lengths of $a$ and $b$ and a hypotenuse with length $c$, then $a squared plus b squared equals c squared$. Substituting $70$ for $a$ and $24$ for $b$ in this equation yields $70 squared plus 24 squared equals c squared$, or $5,476 equals c squared$. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields $plus or minus 74 equals c$. Since the length of the hypotenuse must be positive, $74 equals c$. Therefore, the length of $upper X upper Y$ is $74$ units. The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of all sides. Thus, $left parenthesis 74 plus 70 plus 24 right parenthesis$ units, or $168$ units, is the perimeter of triangle $upper X upper Y upper Z$.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This would be the perimeter, in units, for a right triangle where the length of side $upper Y upper Z$ is $12$ units, not $24$ units.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
